/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  LABBAN 2017 -- NaCl 1000 mg/kg at pH 7 through the LbL-C membrane

  LbL-C hollow-fibre NF membrane, single salt NaCl 1000 mg/kg, pH 7.0 (the membrane's isoelectric
  point, p. 19), observed rejection at 1, 2 and 3 bar.
  REJECTION: Fig. 7 (manuscript p. 20, journal p. 25), the up-triangles (pH = 7.0), centroid of each
  marker read from the figure at 400 dpi: 0.135, 0.196, 0.241.  At 1 bar the pH 7 and pH 8 symbols
  overlap and are drawn as one star: the star's centre (0.135) is read for both.  DIGITISED,
  reading uncertainty +-0.004 (marker centroid, triangle offset).
  FEED: 1000 mg/kg / 58.44 g/mol (catalogue NaCl record) = 17.11 mol/m3.
  FLUX: NOT reported for these points.  Taken from the pure-water line of Fig. 6 (manuscript p. 19),
  digitised: slope 10.30 LMH/bar = 2.862e-6 m/s/bar, J_v = 2.862e-6 (dP - 0.077 bar) =
  2.642e-6, 5.504e-6, 8.366e-6 m/s at 1, 2, 3 bar.  This IGNORES the osmotic back-pressure of the salt
  (about 0.1 bar at 1 bar), so the flux is up to ~10 %% HIGH at 1 bar: an ASSUMPTION of this case.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     membrane.rejection;
membrane     LbLC;

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus digitisedFromFigure;
    citation     "O. Labban, C. Liu, T. H. Chong, J. H. Lienhard V, Fundamentals of low-pressure nanofiltration: Membrane characterization, modeling, and understanding the multi-ionic interactions in water softening, J. Membr. Sci. 521 (2017) 18-32, doi:10.1016/j.memsci.2016.08.062, Figure 7 (rejection) and Figure 6 (flux)";
    identity     "one series of the study cited above (accepted manuscript read page by page as images and the journal version for the tables); no doi identity of its own";
    licence      "facts: numbers transcribed from a published article (Elsevier copyright); the article and its figures are not in the tree";
}

T            298.15 K;     // ASSUMED: the article states no temperature (see the case README)
feed         { NaCl 17.1116 mol/m3; }

columns
(
    { name Jv;  unit m/s; }
    { name R_NaCl;  unit -; }
);

data
(
    2.642000e-06  0.1350
    5.504000e-06  0.1960
    8.366000e-06  0.2410
);
